Adapt to a current system: the xlock menus list the original modes that
the installed xlockmore still has (the old maketemp(`TMPDIR/...') never
expanded TMPDIR, and current xlock -help lists ~140 modes with their
options); the pointer is centered with WarpToWindow (absolute CursorMove
is gone); Restart reuses fvwm's arguments (the bootstrap); menu entries
for removed modules are dropped, Window List uses FvwmIconMan; Msgs runs
journalctl, Help opens with xdg-open, Root shell uses su -; SeaMonkey
and Firefox next to Netscape.

diff --git a/.fvwm2rc.defines b/.fvwm2rc.defines
index a71ee96..815dffe 100644
--- a/.fvwm2rc.defines
+++ b/.fvwm2rc.defines
@@ -55,7 +55,9 @@ define(`XRELEASE',`6')
 # Uncomment for auto generation of xlock/screensaver options-- useful if your
 # xlock produces a standard usage message for the -h option.
 # Comment it to use either the R5 or R6 standard choices (depends on XRELEASE, above)
-define(`AUTO_XLOCK_OPTIONS')
+# Current xlockmore has well over 100 modes, too many for one menu, so this
+# is off; the standard choices only list the modes the installed xlock has.
+#define(`AUTO_XLOCK_OPTIONS')
 
 # Uncomment for auto generation of host menu-- uses /etc/hosts.
 # Comment if you're using NIS, yp, or if you just have a big /etc/hosts file
@@ -83,8 +85,8 @@ define(`MIDI_SOUND_PATH',`/E/sound/midi')
 # BROSWER_HELP_COMMAND is what to run to show the help for the configuration
 # (You may want to use netscape or mosaic instead of arena, at least until
 # arena matures a bit)
-define(`WWW_BROWSER',`arena')
-define(`HELP_FILE',`/usr/local/lib/fvwm-config/docs/index.html')
+define(`WWW_BROWSER',`xdg-open')
+define(`HELP_FILE',`/usr/share/doc/packages/thenextlevel/docs/index.html')
 define(`BROSWER_HELP_COMMAND',WWW_BROWSER HELP_FILE)
 
 # Comment the define directly above, and use this instead if you're want
@@ -179,7 +181,10 @@ define(`USE_CLOSE_FOR_DECORATIONS')
 # Comment below if you don't want to be able to start a tail -f 
 # of a message log in an rxvt from SystemUtils menu
 # Change it to the most appropriate general log on your system
-define(`MESSAGE_LOG',`/var/log/messages')
+#define(`MESSAGE_LOG',`/var/log/messages')
+# Command for the Msgs entry; it wins over MESSAGE_LOG. Systems with
+# systemd have no /var/log/messages.
+define(`MESSAGES_COMMAND',`journalctl -f -n 8')
 
 
 # Change the BORDER_WIDTH to be the number of pixels in a window frame.
